VALUES (
  57,
  'Why Do Children Become Disobedient? Essential Guidance for Parents ....',
  'why-do-children-become-disobedient-essential-guidance-for-parents',
  'Why Do Children Become Disobedient? Essential Guidance for Parents Introduction Nowadays, many parents complain that their children don''t listen to them, show disrespect at home, a',
  '<span id="docs-internal-guid-1b1e8ea7-7fff-8cf3-a662-eba14fb91741"><p dir="ltr" style="line-height:1.38;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="border-width: initial; border-style: none; border-color: initial; display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; width: 624px; height: 305px;"><img src="/images/blogs/why-do-children-become-disobedient-essential-guidance-for-parents-content-1.jpeg" width="624" height="305" style="text-align: left; margin-left: 0px; margin-top: 0px;"></span></span></p><h1 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 24pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 24pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Why Do Children Become Disobedient? Essential Guidance for Parents</span></h1><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 24pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Introduction</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Nowadays, many parents complain that their children don''t listen to them, show disrespect at home, and feel distant from their parents. But have you ever wondered why this distance is being created? Why don''t children feel that closeness with their parents that should be there? Why can''t they share each other''s personal lives?</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">These questions are very important because until we understand the root of the problem, we cannot find its solution.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Main Reasons for Disobedience in Children</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Parents'' Busy Schedules and Lack of Time</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">The biggest problem is that in today''s era, parents are so busy that finding time for their children has become difficult. Office work, business, and daily responsibilities are so overwhelming that parents cannot spend quality time with their children.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">It is the children''s right to have time allocated for them. In the Quran, Allah says: </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">"يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قُوا أَنفُسَكُمْ وَأَهْلِيكُمْ "</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> (O you who believe! Protect yourselves and your families from the fire of hell. But unfortunately, we are unable to fulfil this responsibility.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">I personally witnessed an incident where a father would leave at 7 AM and return at 11 PM. The child would already be asleep. He could only see his child on Sundays throughout the week. Now tell me, how can this child connect with his father?</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Lack of Proper Environment at Home</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">The second major problem is that even when family members are at home, everyone is busy with their own tasks. Father is on the mobile phone, mother is in the kitchen or watching TV, and children are playing games in their rooms.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Even while living at home, every person is so engrossed in their own work 24 hours a day that conversations don''t happen. The culture of family dinners has ended. There''s no time to sit together and talk.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said: </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">"خَيْرُكُمْ خَيْرُكُمْ لِأَهْلِهِ وَأَنَا خَيْرُكُمْ لِأَهْلِي"</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> (The best among you is the one who is best to his family, and I am the best among you to my family).</span></h2><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="border-width: initial; border-style: none; border-color: initial; display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; width: 624px; height: 305px;"><img src="/images/blogs/why-do-children-become-disobedient-essential-guidance-for-parents-content-2.jpeg" width="624" height="305" style="text-align: left; margin-left: 0px; margin-top: 0px;"></span></span></p><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Ignoring Children''s Nature</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Children have a natural disposition. If we work according to their nature, many things become easy. A child learns by watching, learns by listening, but most of all, they adopt what they see.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">For example, understand it this way: when a baby is born, they don''t know any language. But within two to three years, they gradually begin to speak. Why? Because they keep hearing, keep watching. They were never told, ''This is Urdu; this is English; this is Arabic. '' They learn from the environment.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Similarly, if you want your child to be obedient, you must also respect your own parents. Children will watch from the front.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Distance from Religious Education</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Another major problem is that children are kept away from religious education. They are not taught what the status of parents is, what respect for elders means, or how life should be lived.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">When a child isn''t told who their role model should be, they will choose one themselves. It might be some singer, some actor, or some other worldly personality, regardless of what kind of character that person has.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">The child gradually learns the bad things about society. If society is oppressive, they will also become oppressive. Tomorrow, this same oppression will be inflicted on their parents, on their society.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><br></h3><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 8pt 0pt 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="border-width: initial; border-style: none; border-color: initial; display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; width: 624px; height: 305px;"><img src="/images/blogs/why-do-children-become-disobedient-essential-guidance-for-parents-content-3.jpeg" width="624" height="305" style="text-align: left; margin-left: 0px; margin-top: 0px;"></span></span></p><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 18pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">What is the solution? What Should Parents Do?</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Spend Quality Time</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">First and most important, make time for your children. Half an hour daily, or even 20 minutes, but spend that time only with your kids. Turn off your mobile, turn off the TV, and just talk to your children.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">At least one day a week, spend time with the whole family. Eat together, listen to their conversations, and know their difficulties. This small habit can bring a huge change.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">One of my friends adopted this formula: every night before sleeping, he would sit with his children for 15 minutes. The children would share their day, and he would listen. In just 6 months, there was a clear difference in the children''s personalities.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Provide Religious and Moral Education</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 26pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Teach your children religion and explain to them the basic principles of life. Make them understand what respect for elders means and in what manner they should talk to younger ones. Explain with practical examples what the high status of parents is in Islam and what the rights of teachers are. Also, gradually teach them how to live as responsible citizens in society.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Tell them the blessed Seerah of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ,&nbsp; how His childhood was spent, and how He showed loving treatment toward His uncle Abu Talib. Narrate incidents from the lives of the noble companions, and tell stories of the simplicity and piety of the righteous scholars.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">When these things are taught in childhood, they become firm in the heart and mind. One can learn later too, but that''s not as strong. What is learned in childhood stays for a lifetime.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 2pt 0pt 4pt;"><br></h2><p dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 8pt 0pt 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="border-width: initial; border-style: none; border-color: initial; display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; width: 624px; height: 305px;"><img src="/images/blogs/why-do-children-become-disobedient-essential-guidance-for-parents-content-4.jpeg" width="624" height="305" style="text-align: left; margin-left: 0px; margin-top: 0px;"></span></span></p><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Become a Role Model Yourself</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Remember, children don''t learn from your words; they learn from your character. If you want your child to pray, pray regularly yourself. If you want them to speak the truth, speak the truth yourself.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">I remember an incident when a child asked his father, "Dad,</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> you tell me not to lie, but yesterday you said on the phone that you were in the car when you were actually sitting at home."</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> The father had no answer.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Choose the Right </span><a href="https://www.ajwaacademy.com" style="text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Online Quran Teacher</span></a></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Very busy parents can take help from an online Quran teacher. But caution is necessary here, too. Don''t just grab anyone randomly.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 22pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">If you want your child to learn the Quran online, choose an instructor who is fully trained themselves. Someone who has deep knowledge not just of the Quran but also of Hadith. Along with that, they should be familiar with Fiqh and Islamic law so they can provide proper guidance to the child. And most importantly, they should understand child psychology, have the ability to teach according to the child''s temperament, and teach how to adopt religion in practical life, not just recite words.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Today, many families are enrolling their children in </span><a href="https://www.ajwaacademy.com" style="text-decoration:none;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">online Quran classes</span></a><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> because of the flexibility and access to qualified scholars from anywhere in the world. Especially for online Quran classes for kids, the teacher must know how to keep young learners engaged and motivated.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Ajwa Academy''s Role</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">At Ajwa Academy, we understand that religion is not just about reading words. All our teachers have received formal religious education for 10 to 12 years. They are not merely Huffaz but complete Islamic scholars who are familiar with every aspect of religion.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">We offer structured online Quran courses designed to build both knowledge and character. Whether your child wants to memorise the Quran online or simply understand its meanings, our qualified online Quran tutors are here to guide them step by step.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Our fundamental mission is that children don''t just read the words of the Quran but also understand its meanings and concepts. We want them to know the rights of their parents and fulfil them with complete honesty. How to behave at home, how to treat siblings, and how to respect teachers and elders – we teach all of this practically through our Quran lessons online.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 10pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Our tutors provide regular, detailed reports to parents. These reports don''t just tell how many Surahs the child has memorised or how many pages they''ve read, but they also include details about improvements in the child''s morals and character.</span></h3><h3 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><br></h3><h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="border-width: initial; border-style: none; border-color: initial; display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; width: 624px; height: 305px;"><img src="/images/blogs/why-do-children-become-disobedient-essential-guidance-for-parents-content-5.jpeg" width="624" height="305" style="text-align: left; margin-left: 0px; margin-top: 0px;"></span></span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 26pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Practical Tips</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Here are some easy tips you can start implementing today.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">First of all, spend just 15 minutes daily with your children in simple conversation – no scolding or reprimanding. At least one day a week, have a meal with the whole family, sit together, and keep mobile phones completely off.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 16pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Try to have one small recreational trip per month, even if it''s just going to a nearby park, but everyone should be together. Before bedtime, tell stories to your children, especially from the Seerah of the Prophet ﷺ, incidents from the lives of the Companions, and about the lives of righteous scholars. And most importantly, become a role model yourself. Whatever you want to teach, practise it yourself first.</span></h2><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.656; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 16pt; padding: 14pt 0pt 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Conclusion</span></h2><ul style="padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1"><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 30pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Children don''t become disobedient; we make them so. When we don''t give time, don''t pay attention, and don''t teach religion, they create their own path.</span></h2></li><li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1"><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Remember that what you invest in your child today will become your support tomorrow. When you grow old, become sick, or are in need, this same child will stand with you.</span></h2></li><li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1"><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">But this is only possible when you are with them today; teach them religion, teach them morals.</span></h2></li><li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1"><h2 dir="ltr" style="text-align: left; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; padding: 0pt 0pt 16pt;" role="presentation"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Whether the child becomes a scientist, doctor, or engineer, first and foremost, they must become a good human being. And there''s only one way to become a good person: living life according to nature and Shariah.</span></h2></li></ul><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><div style="text-align: left;" bis_skin_checked="1"><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">Contact Ajwa Academy today and give your children the education that makes them successful in both this world and the hereafter. Start with our </span><a href="https://www.ajwaacademy.com/courses" style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; text-decoration: none;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;, serif; color: rgb(17, 85, 204); background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;">online Quran classes</span></a><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline;"> and take the first step toward raising a generation that is both knowledgeable and righteous.</span></div></span></span>',
